From fe7c719d91c94ca5a50cb60653b91d909b344383 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:55:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ExactPredicates: generated kernels instead of BigInteger
 beyond the expansion range (#711)

Orient2d, Orient3d and InCircle on coordinates outside [2^-100, 2^100] used a BigInteger
determinant on a common power-of-two scale (1 to 30 us and 1.4 to 12 KB per call for spans of
hundreds of binary orders). They now call the kernels of DoublePredicates. The *_bigint
functions stay as the reference of the tests and as InSphere's exact stage.

The 61 fuzz units of issue #711 (master a7693fd, 4 cores): 289.4 -> 51.3 s, median 4.04 ->
0.61 s, maximum 14.0 -> 2.2 s, none above 5 s (18 before), 243 -> 12 GB allocated; result hash,
status, RoundingClean and all counts equal in 61 of 61. Normal operations do not change (the
stage is not reached). benchmarks/PredicateComparison gets the mode 'span'.

ExactPredicatesBeyondRangeTests: no allocation on the fallback, and a unit of #711 with a
bound on the operation's allocation (43 MB; 1.9 GB before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AaGT5CdtKaF4p9ewMMrjAm
